        "CopyrightInformation": "All material appearing in this report is in the public domain and may be reproduced or copied without permission; citation as to source, however, is appreciated.",
        "AbstractText": "Key findings Data from the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey ● In 2015-2016, the prevalence of obesity was 39.8% in adults and 18.5% in youth. ● The prevalence of obesity was higher among middle-aged adults (42.8%) than among younger adults (35.7%). ● The prevalence of obesity was higher among youth aged 6-11 years (18.4%) and adolescents aged 12-19 years (20.6%) compared with children aged 2-5 years (13.9%). ● The overall prevalence of obesity was higher among non-Hispanic black and Hispanic adults than among non-Hispanic white and non-Hispanic Asian adults. The same pattern was seen among youth. ● The observed change in prevalence between 2013-2014 and 2015-2016 was not significant among both adults and youth."
